  "reason": "All four completed experiments used singleprofile; the current best (config_022: multimodal, pca_n2000, vit_l, concat, acc=0.535) has not been tested with multiprofile. The single biggest unexplored design dimension is profile setting, and if multiprofile aggregation provides complementary information across profiles, it could yield a meaningful accuracy gain. config_024 is the most direct extension of config_022—changing only singleprofile→multiprofile with the simplest aggregation (avgpool)—so it cleanly isolates the multiprofile effect while keeping the proven RNA encoder, image encoder, and fusion strategy fixed. If multiprofile helps, the remaining 5 experiments can explore transformer aggregation and weighted fusion; if it does not, we can redirect budget toward RNA encoder variants (scvi, scgpt) or fusion changes. This is the highest-information experiment available under the remaining budget."
}

